<title>INDIA: India approves Shinawatra International's plans.</title>
<headline>India approves Shinawatra International's plans.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's Industry Ministry on Monday approved a proposal by Thailand's telecommunications firm Shinawatra International to set up a 100 percent holding company, a government statement said.</p>
<p>The company will bring in foreign direct investment worth 3.5 billion rupees ($98 million), it added.</p>
<p>Shinawatra International is a unit of Thailand's Shinawatra Computer and Communications plc.</p>
<p>The Industry Ministry approved 83 foreign proposals worth 13.66 billion rupees ($381 million), the statement said. ($1 = 35.85 rupees)</p>
<p>--New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
